WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Picture a paper mill on a riverbank.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.060
It pays for its wood,

3
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.340
its workers and its energy.

4
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.670
Every bill, on time.

5
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.140
Buyers want its paper.

6
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.970
Supply meets demand.

7
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.420
The market looks perfectly healthy.

8
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.990
Yet economists say this
market makes too much paper,

9
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.780
even though the mill
gets its own sums right.

10
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.050
So why does a factory
that pays all its own

11
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.760
bills still produce too much?

12
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.350
In this mission, you'll
draw the diagram that shows

13
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.770
the gap between the market
and the social optimum.

14
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.350
Then you'll turn a slider
and watch a triangle

15
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.780
of welfare loss change size.

16
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.040
Your mission: find out
what the market leaves out,

17
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.030
and what it costs society.
